# S3 side test (2026-10-28): is the 40-epoch cosine too long for the arms without JC?
# SC peaks at epoch 11 and FT <- P0 at epochs 5-7 of 40, with the lr still ~85% of its
# peak, and then overfit; the JC arms peak later (SC + JC 10-14, FT + JC and FR + JC 26-40).
# The S3 winners of SC and FT <- P0 again, with a 15-epoch cosine that anneals near
# their peak. Compare with their 40-epoch S3 runs (S3_lr_20261026_100949: 0.6238, 0.6297);
# a clear gain argues for a per-arm epoch budget in the final runs.
#
#   ENCODERS=rowcol_concat_v0 CHUNK=512 SEEDS=42 PACKS=1 MEM_PER_GPU_GB=22 \
#   MAX_EPOCHS=15 EST_SECONDS_PER_EPOCH=1250 WALLTIME=1-00:00:00 \
#   CELLS=scripts/configs/campaign/S3_epochs.cells bash slurm/ssl_pack.sh
sc_lr1.1e-3_ep15  arm=scratch encoders=${ENCODERS} chunk_size=${CHUNK} datamodule.batch_size=28672 optimizer.lr=1.1e-3
ft_p0_lr2.2e-3_bb10_ep15  arm=finetune encoder_ckpt=@/storage3/DSIP/rriva/research/fm4tag-chunk/slurm/ssl_campaign/P_full_20261023_085735/p0/seed_42 encoders=${ENCODERS} chunk_size=${CHUNK} datamodule.batch_size=28672 optimizer.lr=2.2e-3 optimizer.backbone_lr=2.2e-4
